// EXPECT-RUNTIME-ERROR: cannot compare string and string
//
// Ordering comparisons are numeric-only (the VM's OPCODE_LT/GT/LE/GE family).
// The type checker currently lets `"a" < "b"` through, so this is where the
// language says no; the C backend used to answer `false` instead, which turned an
// unsupported operation into a plausible-looking wrong answer (S14).
//
// Whoever tightens the checker to reject ordering on strings at compile time
// should move this case to tests/conformance/ui/ — the runtime error must stay
// reachable for bytecode that does not come from this front end.
fn main() {
    print("a" < "b")
}
